# NextSync configuration -- copy to the drawer NextSync lives in,
# rename to NextSync.conf, and fill in your own details.
#
# You do not have to write this by hand. Start NextSync with no
# configuration and it opens Preferences, where Connect lists the folders
# on your account for you to pick from. This file is what it writes.
#
# Prefer a Nextcloud *app password* (Settings -> Security on the server)
# over your account password: this file is plain text on the Amiga.

server  cloud.example.com
port    443
user    yourname
pass    your-app-password

# The drawer the synced folders are kept in. Created if it is missing.

local   DH0:Nextcloud

# One line per folder in your Nextcloud file root that you want synced.
# "folder Documents" keeps DH0:Nextcloud/Documents in step with
# /Documents on the server, subfolders and all.

folder  Documents
# folder  Photos

# For a folder that has to live somewhere else, an explicit pair still
# works, and Preferences leaves it alone when it saves:
#
# pair    /Photos    Work:Cloud/Pictures
